From 078fd885cf0c542af8328361c69f334d8083d04a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Johnathon Selstad <makeshifted@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 13:04:54 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] GLTFLoader: Add setLazyLOD() and setRangeRequests().

`setLazyLOD( true )` loads only the coarsest level of each `MSFT_lod`
node before `onLoad()`. The other levels are loaded when `LOD.update()`
asks for them, the nearest ones first and three at the same time, and
the nearest loaded level is rendered until then.

`setRangeRequests( true )` loads binary files with HTTP range requests,
so that the buffer views of levels that are not needed are not
downloaded. The first request is for the first 64 KiB of the file. A
JSON chunk that is longer is read from one open-ended request, which is
cancelled when the bytes that arrive are not needed anymore. The ranges
that are asked for in the same tick are sorted and merged. If the
server answers 200 instead of 206, the file is read once, as it
arrives, and each range is resolved as soon as its bytes are in.

`GLTFParser.loadBufferRange()` is what the meshopt extension now reads
its source bytes with, which lets compressed buffer views be fetched
individually as well.

Both options are off by default.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
